            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0261" n="165" xml:id="pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">368.117/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Greece</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-14T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your 861, November 18, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>Endeavor ascertain whether similar treatment will be accorded naturalized
                    American citizens who complied with American law but were exempted or given
                    deferred classification; also what treatment will be accorded those who have
                    neither served nor registered for service because not within military age,
                    absent from country or other satisfactory reason, especially in view pending
                    naturalization Convention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
